    doc+='</section><section id="geometry"><h2>Unchanged parser, checker and palette; proposed blank workspace</h2><p>The fixed tree instruction program completed each exact selected request. A separately written stack interpreter independently reproduced every instruction/event/profile and every canonical heap node. Record widths are calculated exactly, including the sentinel and trailing blank. These complete deterministic heap estimates do not certify any unselected request or every other tape band, and do not replace native microcode execution.</p>'+layout(obs[7]['original_initial'],obs[7]['proposed_initial'])+'<p>Only the proposed external blank capacity of heap band <code>26</code> changes from 73,178 to 262,144. Every initial word and local head stays byte-identical; later physical bands move by the added 188,966 blanks. The independent auditor reconstructs every original and proposed encoded input byte and physical band displacement. No semantic checker instruction, symbol alphabet, parser, universal tile palette or mathematical premise changes.</p>'+table(['Selected request','Original physical width','Proposed physical width','Proposed input SHA-256'],[(a['query']+1,n(a['physical_width_before']),n(a['physical_width_after']),a['proposed_input_sha256']) for a in audit['observations']])+'<p class="pin">Fixed program SHA-256: '+audit['program_sha256']+'. Fixed microtable SHA-256: '+audit['micro_sha256']+'.</p></section>'
    doc+='<section id="costs"><h2>Separate resource ledger</h2>'+table(['Component','Seconds','Peak RSS bytes','Native queries'],[('Eight selected fixed-program capacity estimates',sec(summary['seconds']),n(summary['peak_rss_bytes']),0),('Independent complete selected-request replay/encoding',sec(audit['seconds']),n(audit['peak_rss_bytes']),0)])+'<p>Both processes used a 180-second / 512 MiB ceiling. Each selected estimate had a 20-million tree-instruction and 200,000-node ceiling; proposed physical heap capacity was capped at 1,048,576 cells. No ceiling was raised and no native admission batch started. These are shared-host resource-study measurements, not a cluster-search speed claim.</p><p>The first complete grammar attempt’s memory-budget unknown, fresh retry and independent audit costs remain in <a href="commutativity_feasibility.html#costs">the immutable feasibility ledger</a>. All prior zero-left and left-successor theorem discovery, admission, certification and unknown costs remain in their existing readers. The separate entire-catalog retry correspondence inspection adds 5.479 seconds; it confirms unchanged grammar payloads except measured build time and a descriptive compaction tag. Manual infrastructure work remains unmeasured.</p><p>Any small native pilot is a separately frozen next gate after this audit. It must use these exact reconstructed inputs, preserve unknown/rejected outcomes and account for complete independent native replay. The unselected 86 capacity estimates and all unresolved native interfaces remain explicit; no 93-query batch is authorized by this supplement.</p></section>'
